# Cloudflare Workers static-assets header rules (served by the ASSETS binding).
# https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/static-assets/headers
# https://opennext.js.org/cloudflare/caching#static-assets-caching
#
# Long-lived immutable caching for the site's STABLE, content-stable public
# assets: 3D models + their seamless posters, per-page OG images, brand marks
# and client logos, and the AR QR SVG (under /models). Without a rule the
# Workers assets runtime serves these with `public, max-age=0, must-revalidate`,
# forcing a revalidation round-trip on every load — so the prefetched 4.4 MB GLB
# and posters never benefit from disk caching on repeat views.
#
# CAVEAT — immutable means clients keep a cached copy for up to a year keyed on
# the URL. Any REPLACEMENT of an asset at the SAME filename (e.g. regenerating
# sheen-chair.glb, or the real Thridify SDK model landing at an old name) will
# NOT be picked up by returning visitors. Asset replacements MUST change the
# filename or append a ?v= query (versioned filenames for the real SDK embed /
# new client models). See docs/ASSET-DEBT.md.
#
# NOTE: /_next/static/* is deliberately NOT listed here — its handling is out of
# scope for this change (see ASSET-DEBT caching entry).

/models/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/og/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/brand/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/logos/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
